WEBVTT

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.020
<i>12 seconds?</i>

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.550
<i>That's almost five seconds faster than me!</i>

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:39.640
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.000
<b><i> Wall 11    The 15 Second Wall</i></b>

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.370
Hey.

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:55.840
U-Uh, I...

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:57.590
You!

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.570
That's a nice hairpin. Let me try it on.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:03.720
O-Okay.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.230
How's it look?

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:10.060
Uh... Cute, I think.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:12.540
Aw yeah, that's hype!

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.270
Er, what were you saying?

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:18.240
U-Uh, so, after I saw how fast you climb,

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:22.390
I wanted to ask what you focus on.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:26.000
I know you can't give a 
rival that information,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.600
but I really want to know...

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:30.890
Okay!

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:32.880
Huh? Are you sure?

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.180
Yeah, sure. You did call me cute and all.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:40.010
I'm Takahashi Mimu. Call me Mimu.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.000
Oh, okay.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.750
You wanna know what I focus on when I climb?

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:45.770
Yes.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.520
The answer is rhythm games!

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:54.900
Rhythm games?

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:59.680
I've always liked grooving to a beat.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.910
I'm a climber first, 
but I also dabble in dance.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.490
I see speed climbing 
as a game where you gotta

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:09.410
time the holds right as 
they scroll down past you.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:12.420
A game where you gotta time the holds right?

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.420
Yup.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.890
I believe it's important 
to maintain your tempo.

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:21.820
It'd suck if I tried to climb too fast, 
screwed up my rhythm, and lost time.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.940
It'd be no fun to climb like that, anyway.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:28.580
The key is your tempo and spacing,
 your very own rhythm.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.820
Thank you very much!

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.790
Go get it, Miss Puzzle Piece.

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:53.040
Jun-chan!

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:55.960
I got it! It's ta-ta-tan!

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:56.940
What?

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:00.710
Ta-ta-tan, ta-ta-ta!

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:01.660
Ta?

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:06.790
<i>From the start to five hands up...</i>

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:11.290
<i>This part goes ta, ta-ta-tan.</i>

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:13.980
<i>Nah, hang on.</i>

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:17.730
<i>If I can grab the third hold 
with Ooba-san's perfect posture,</i>

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.530
<i>I can go ta, ta-tan.</i>

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:25.100
<i>Their techniques are blending
 into my rhythm.</i>

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:27.000
<i>They're grooving to my beat!</i>

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:34.540
I did it!

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:39.470
All right, then.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:43.420
We'll measure your times for the last 
time this camp under race conditions.

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:45.820
I'm up against...

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:47.180
Me.

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.450
On your marks, ready...

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:05.390
Huh? She's way faster than yesterday!

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:08.320
She's keeping up with Ooba-san, 
who clocks in around 15 seconds!

00:05:08.670 --> 00:05:10.330
<i>Looking good, Konomi.</i>

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:14.330
That's a nice beat. Makes me wanna dance.

00:05:14.330 --> 00:05:16.330
<i>Ta, ta-ta-tan-tan!</i>

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.330
<i>I'm grooving!</i>

00:05:18.950 --> 00:05:20.840
<i>This is my rhythm!</i>

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:22.340
<i>I see.</i>

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:26.640
<i>I should've seen this coming. 
She has made the moves her own.</i>

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:28.340
<i>But it isn't enough.</i>

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:31.350
<i>My climbing won't be bested that easily!</i>

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.350
They're almost to the top, they are!

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:35.820
Who's going to win?!

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:43.610
It was close, but Ooba takes this race.

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:50.010
<i>She's suddenly become competitive in speed.</i>

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:55.620
<i>Not even my best was enough to beat Ooba-san.</i>

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:57.850
<i>I really wanted to win that.</i>

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:58.620
Konomi!

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:00.400
Jun-chan?

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.200
Look up!

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:01.750
Up?

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:11.560
Yes! I made it under 15 seconds!

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:13.010
Way to go, Konomi.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.360
That's faster than me.

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:17.890
I've got some catching up to do, I do.

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:22.650
<i>I wasn't expecting her to 
improve her time that much.</i>

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:25.980
<i>But I will keep winning.</i>

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.320
<i>That's my Jun-chan!</i>

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.990
<i>Hanamiya now has a real shot at 
winning the team championship.</i>

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:44.570
Girls, you did incredibly well 
over these last three days.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.600
You're all wonderful!

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.770
You're all truly beautiful!

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:52.360
Please don't forget that!

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:53.390
And with that,

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.120
the speed climbing camp is over!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.890
Thank you very much.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:01.740
What's he crying fur?

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.460
He's a nice guy, he is.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.900
Mimu-san.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:08.560
Puzzle-chan!

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:11.390
You looked really good back there.

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:14.110
All thanks to your advice.

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:16.200
Thank you again.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.410
Aw, don't mention it.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:22.480
It got me vibin', so it's a win-win.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:26.420
A full combo of happiness, a AAA best score!

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.420
R-Right...

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.620
Anyway, I should get going.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:32.010
Oh, okay.

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:34.600
Laters!

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.850
Cool Kurusu.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:45.230
<i>Kokureikan... Anne-san's high school...</i>

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:50.890
Oh, you're entering the upcoming 
Combined Japan High School Cup, right?

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:52.330
R-Right.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.680
We'll see each other again there.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:54.590
Yeah.

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:55.630
Bye bye!

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:56.600
Uh...

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:00.000
She goes to Kokureikan?

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:06.070
Unless we beat both Anne-san 
and Mimu-san, we...

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.780
Hanamiya can't win.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.430
That's right.

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:13.930
Not much time left.
 We've gotta make full use of it.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:17.010
Yeah.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.590
Together, as a team.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:26.860
I've been waiting for you, my dear juniors.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:29.560
Let my loving embrace envelop you.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.360
I-I can't breathe!

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:33.530
You got your time under 15 seconds, huh?

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:34.560
Yeah!

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:35.980
You did well.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:39.210
What were you up to while we were gone?

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:42.540
Nono-san?

00:08:43.400 --> 00:08:45.590
Why'd you have to remind me?

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:49.830
All day, every day, Sayo-chin 
was a teacher from hell

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:52.900
and made me study up on climbing 
in one-on-one sessions.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:58.740
Ugh, I felt like I was cramming 
for my entrance exams.

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:01.770
But it helped, didn't it?

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:04.200
She's here! Hell Teacher Sayo-chin!

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:05.640
Welcome back.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.730
Kiku-chan?

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:11.050
She wants to observe our team for a while.

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:12.030
Really?

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:16.330
She'll be helping us with 
tournament prep, correct?

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:18.780
Yeah. Thanks for having me.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:21.540
You're always welcome, Kiku-chan!

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.620
Let's get right to practice, then.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:25.540
Yeah!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:29.980
Nice!

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:31.550
Nice, Jun-chan.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:33.070
Uehara-san...

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:35.240
Does she seem better than 
the last time you saw her?

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:36.050
Yeah.

00:09:37.010 --> 00:09:41.440
For a while after the 
tournament you came to watch,

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.310
she couldn't climb at all.

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:47.810
But that adversity gave her 
the push she needed to grow.

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:51.320
Even Nono, who was in tears last time,

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:55.070
has worked hard to get over that hump.

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:57.790
She's short and lacks reach,

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:01.700
but she's made up for it with 
her resilient mentality.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.700
She's climbed walls over and over again,

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:06.960
and tirelessly practiced her grabbing moves.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:08.960
And...

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:10.960
<i>Tan-ta-tan, ta-tan-tan.</i>

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:12.960
<i>Tsh-tsh-ta!</i>

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:15.710
Konomi-san has conquered her weakness.

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.970
Wow, Master.

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:21.970
They're all so amazing.

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:28.420
Say, Sayo-chin.

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.980
Did something happen 
during practice today?

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.760
Huh? What do you mean?

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:35.480
You had this sad look on your face.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.770
Sad? Why would I?

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:40.490
I have nothing to be sad about.

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.850
Forget about me. How are you doing?

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:46.480
Urk... Slow and steady, I guess?

00:10:46.480 --> 00:10:48.040
"Slow"?

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:52.760
But hey, since you taught me so much 
about dealing with my weaknesses,

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:55.400
I'm having a lot of fun climbing these days.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:58.300
You really opened my eyes in a bunch of ways.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:00.010
Is that so? I'm glad to hear it.

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:04.140
I'm gonna use everything I've learned 
in the upcoming competition.

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:07.640
Great.

00:11:20.210 --> 00:11:21.940
She's quick.

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:23.030
Yeah.

00:11:26.030 --> 00:11:28.140
That was awesome, Captain.

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:31.340
You're sure to lead Hanamiya to victory.

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:33.040
Thank you, Kiku-chan.

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:35.290
Sayo-chin.

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:38.550
Can we talk?

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.550
Huh? Sure.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:47.500
What's happening? Nono-senpai 
seemed mad about something.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:52.560
What is it?

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:53.980
Sayo-chin...

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:55.810
What's wrong with you?

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:57.370
Nono?

00:11:57.370 --> 00:12:00.730
Why'd you start practicing 
speed climbing all of a sudden?

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:04.070
Didn't you say you would 
skip the Combined Cup?

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:08.580
Your injury hasn't fully healed yet!

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:11.710
That's not true.

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:17.020
You saw me climb, didn't you? 
I clocked in at 13 seconds.

00:12:17.020 --> 00:12:19.420
My finger is as good as—

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:22.360
Yeah, no! You were climbing all weird!

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:23.340
Weird?

00:12:23.340 --> 00:12:26.970
I can tell! I've watched you for years!

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:34.230
Didn't your doctor say you might have 
to retire if you aggravate your injury?

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:38.860
You always said you wanted to 
climb all your life, remember?

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:42.860
You want to go pro, don't you? 
You can't take any risks right now, then!

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:47.370
I don't need you to tell me that!

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:52.870
I know that better than anyone. But...

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:57.210
Jun came back to us, 
Konomi-san's improved so much,

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.500
Kiku-chan offered to help the team...

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:05.630
And, most of all, you're really 
enjoying climbing now.

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:10.510
Looking at you made me...

00:13:11.080 --> 00:13:12.770
Sayo-chin.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:17.550
Listen, Nono, I want to climb with this team.

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:20.020
I don't want to be the only one left out!

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:25.150
I mean, this is my last chance 
to climb with you all!

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:31.410
I don't care if I can never climb again...

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:35.290
Das vy am zdobin yoo!

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:38.040
Nono?

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:40.290
No mean no...

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:44.340
I don wan zee imin taken aweh from yoo!

00:13:46.160 --> 00:13:48.300
I won't let it happen!

00:13:52.400 --> 00:13:55.810
I'm the vice captain.

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:59.810
I promise I'll lead the team to victory.

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.040
So, please!

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.080
As you say, Nono.

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.140
I wonder what they're talking about.

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:18.910
Sugiura-senpai had a scary look on her face.

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:19.980
Yeah.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:20.960
Oh.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.440
They're back.

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:26.440
I have an announcement to make.

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:29.840
I won't be entering the upcoming cup.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:35.350
My finger hasn't fully healed yet.

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:38.080
But... without you...

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:41.230
Oh, I'm not worried about that.

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:45.200
I've watched you three grow so much recently.

00:14:45.200 --> 00:14:47.270
I believe you stand a real chance.

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:52.490
One and a half months to go.
 I'll do everything I can to help you prepare...

00:14:52.880 --> 00:14:54.480
with Kiku-chan here.

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:56.160
Right!

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:59.500
I'll be the best support staff...
 I'll try to be.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:15.440
Nono, you've solved most of your problems.

00:15:15.440 --> 00:15:17.890
Heh, yeah.

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:20.810
You're doing a lot better 
than before too, Jun.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:21.900
Yeah.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.650
And Konomi-san's speed time...

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:27.260
It's gone under 14 seconds on average.

00:15:27.260 --> 00:15:28.600
Keep it up.

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:29.610
I will!

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:31.280
You're amazing, Master.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:32.410
Thanks.

00:15:32.920 --> 00:15:34.530
Tomorrow's the day.

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:38.040
Let's do our best to make 
Hanamiya the best in Japan.

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:44.580
What are you waiting for, Kiku-chan?

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.470
Yeah!

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:56.470
Combined Japan 
High School Cup

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:56.470
140?

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.960
That's a lot of participants.

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:02.520
Yes. And that's why, to keep them short,

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:06.550
the prelims this time will be held 
simultaneously in two blocks.

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:11.490
We're in Group B and will go in the 
order of bouldering, speed, and lead.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:13.150
I see.

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:15.960
You seem motivated, Nono.

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:16.810
Of course I am!

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.620
Look, that girl.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:20.960
Hanamiya's Kasahara, right?

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:22.210
That's her?

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:25.800
They're talking about you, Konomi.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:27.130
Y-Yeah.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:30.990
Once this starts for real, 
you'll have even more eyeballs on you.

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:32.040
Can you handle it?

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:35.840
Honestly, it's a bit too much for me.

00:16:36.390 --> 00:16:39.970
But if they're watching me anyway, 
I want to put on a show for them.

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:41.500
That's the spirit.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:43.030
Oh, how purromising.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:47.980
That's how "Murder Observation" 
Kasahara Konomi's gotta be.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:51.370
What do you want, Uchimura? 
Why are you always...

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:53.110
This time, I will win.

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:55.270
Let's meet in the finals!

00:16:56.910 --> 00:17:01.050
Wh-What's with her? She's acting different.

00:17:01.050 --> 00:17:01.820
Yeah.

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:03.000
They're here!

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:04.200
Who?

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:06.500
The favorite to take home this cup.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.280
Kokureikan High!

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:10.000
Anne-chan!

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:14.510
Hey, everyone! I'm here 
to play it cool, Kurusu!

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:16.190
Cool Kurusu!

00:17:16.190 --> 00:17:18.140
Take it home, Kokureikan!

00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:27.640
Oh, it's Kasahara...

00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:28.650
Puzzle-chan!

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:30.320
Told ya we'd meet here.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.470
Mimu-chan.

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:33.600
Let's both break a leg today.

00:17:33.600 --> 00:17:34.650
Y-Yeah.

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:36.060
Laters.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.510
Cool, Kurusu.

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:42.780
Cheer us on, guys.

00:17:42.780 --> 00:17:44.970
Cool Kurusu!

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:48.210
It's time.

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:51.250
The Combined Japan High School Cup

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:54.790
finally begins here and now!

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:57.260
Master...

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:59.550
Getting nervous won't change anything.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:00.970
I know, but...

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:03.850
Let's cheer them on and 
give them the best backing.

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:05.020
Yeah.

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:08.540
<i>All yours, Nono.</i>

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:11.400
First up, the prelims. 
Everyone qualifies, okay?

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:13.020
Okay!

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:17.150
We're going for best in Japan. 
For us, and for Sayo-chin.

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:18.400
Yeah!

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:21.530
The prelims are about to begin.

00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:24.700
Here's Nakata-san, 
the routesetter for this cup.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.740
Glad to be here.

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:30.540
Could you give us a brief 
rundown of the prelim rules?

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:31.820
Sure.

00:18:31.710 --> 00:18:40.550
<b> 8 Problems</b>

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:36.590
The bouldering prelims in this 
cup will follow flashing rules.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:40.550
Climbers will compete on how many problems 
they can solve in the allotted time.

00:18:41.350 --> 00:18:43.960
They're allowed to watch 
other climbers try, right?

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:44.560
Absolutely.

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:47.440
Whoa, just as you see climbers 
dropping like flies...

00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:52.310
Here's the rising star who made a real 
splash in the Kanto Bouldering Championship.

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:57.320
Will Hanamiya Girls' Kasahara 
Konomi be the first to clear?

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:00.460
How will she approach this?

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:03.360
All of these problems seem 
pretty hard for prelims.

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:07.330
The goal here is to whittle the 
numbers down from 140 climbers to 20.

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:10.500
Of course I set difficult problems.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.330
Oh boy!

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:14.740
Has Kasahara entered the observation process?

00:19:15.330 --> 00:19:18.730
It shouldn't be necessary, since you 
have beta in a flashing competition.

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:19.980
Nakata-san?

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:23.340
Yes, but by analyzing the wall up close,

00:19:23.340 --> 00:19:27.230
she must be trying to fine-tune 
the sequence in her mind.

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:30.240
She spends ages analyzing 
and then sends the route in a flash.

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:32.620
That's who Kasahara is.

00:19:32.620 --> 00:19:33.610
I see.

00:19:34.630 --> 00:19:36.610
Kasahara solves the problem!

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:38.350
That's my master!

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:39.610
Well done!

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:42.940
Urgh... "Murder Observation"?

00:19:42.940 --> 00:19:45.150
I was the first to notice her talents.

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:48.680
I should've been the one to give her a 
more fitting, more beautiful moniker.

00:19:48.680 --> 00:19:49.370
What?

00:19:49.760 --> 00:19:51.070
Nice, Konomin.

00:19:51.070 --> 00:19:52.380
Nicely done, Konomi.

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:53.250
Thanks.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.100
Okay, watch me.

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:57.290
I'm going to one-shot this thing, too.

00:19:57.290 --> 00:19:58.000
Right.

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:02.230
There it is! Sugiura Nonoka 
flashes the problem!

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:03.510
Good.

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:07.950
She made up for her lack of height 
with flexibility and sound technique.

00:20:07.950 --> 00:20:09.520
That was expertly done.

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:13.650
Uehara sends it in one again!

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:24.780
The Group B bouldering prelims 
results have just come in.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:29.540
<b>Prelims Group B   Team Scores   Discipline: Bouldering</b>

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:29.540
<b>School            No.      Name      Sends   Zones</b>

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:29.540
<b>E3. Uehara Jun
E4. Kasahara Konomi
E2. Sugiura Nonoka</b>

00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:28.160
The first-placed team in the 
Group B bouldering prelims is...

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:29.540
<b>Hanamiya High</b>

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.540
Hanamiya Girls'!

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:30.780
We're first!

00:20:30.780 --> 00:20:31.520
Yay!

00:20:31.520 --> 00:20:32.190
All right!

00:20:32.190 --> 00:20:34.040
Your seven sends played a big part.

00:20:34.320 --> 00:20:35.760
Next up is speed.

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:37.540
Let's do our best to keep this going.

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:38.960
Yeah!

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.920
<b>A1. Kurusu Anne  Kokureikan High

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:43.420
<b>Ranking  No. 
Name    School  Time</b>

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:43.420
<b>Prelims Group A  Indiv. Scores
  Discipline: Speed</b>

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:43.420
<b>Combined Japan</b>

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:43.420
<b>A1. Kurusu Anne  Kokureikan High
A3. Takahashi Mimu Kokureikan High</b>

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:45.700
Anne-san's first?

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:48.410
She's even faster than Mimu-chan.

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:50.430
They're both in the 11 second range.

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:53.630
The top six places are all Kokureikan's.

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:56.440
We knew this coming in, 
but they really are strong.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.840
Let's go show what we can do, too!

00:21:00.120 --> 00:21:05.710
Fujimura-san, can you give us a 
brief rundown of the speed rules?

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:06.570
Of course.

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:10.730
Climbers will climb two 
identical walls one at a time,

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:13.830
and compete with the field with 
their best time. That's it.

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:17.330
Next up are Hanamiya Girls'

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:19.080
Kasahara Konomi,

00:21:19.080 --> 00:21:22.380
and Kurikawa High's Satou Maruno.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:23.840
On your marks,

00:21:24.230 --> 00:21:25.300
ready...

00:21:33.270 --> 00:21:35.100
<i>She's fast, she is!</i>

00:21:35.990 --> 00:21:37.100
<i>Tan-ta-tan.</i>

00:21:39.720 --> 00:21:41.260
Kasahara has finished.

00:21:42.110 --> 00:21:46.110
Okay, that was perfect. 
It should've been pretty fast.

00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:48.990
<i>That's my personal best.</i>

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:53.720
<i>But it's not even close to 
Mimu-chan and Anne-san's times.</i>

00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:58.650
<i>If this keeps up, there's 
no way Hanamiya can win!</i>

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:04.410
<i>Cool Kurusu!</i>

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.060
<b><i>Iwakakeru!</i></b>

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.060
<b><i>Wall 12: The Road to Best in Japan</i></b>
